== 2.  The degenerate cases: t = 0 and N = 1 ==
  PASS  N=1: Im S_1(t) = 0 identically (1^{-it} = 1 is real; no imaginary part)
  PASS  t = 0 is a TRIVIAL root for every N: Im S_N(0) = -sum sin(0) = 0
  PASS  so the existence statement must be about a POSITIVE height t > 0   [Im S_N(t) < 0 just right of 0 (derivative -sum_{n>=2} log n < 0)]
  PASS  N=1 is therefore degenerate in both senses (root at every t, no t is special)

